      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 86. Toxicity: no fetched page gives any. RHS and NC State name none (NC State only mentions folk medicine for digestion); the ASPCA search page tried returned no plant listings, so that is not a confirmed absence; the ASPCA lavender page found in search is a different plant and was not fetched. Toxicity stays unknown (pets unknown). Hardiness: RHS H5; NC State 6a to 9b. Drought: RHS 'Drought Resistance: Yes', NC State 'good drought tolerance'. Watering style let_fully_dry and 10 days are the agent's mapping and a guess (RHS well-drained or moist but well-drained, NC State good drainage, occasionally to very dry). Size: RHS 0.1 to 0.5 m tall by 0.5 to 1 m wide, NC State 1 to 2 ft by 2 to 3 ft; 50 by 90 cm is the agent's pick. Placement: RHS lists container use; ground from the starter-list row. No RHS growing guide was found for santolina. Missouri Botanical Garden failed twice (certificate error). The quoted wording came back through a summarising fetch and was not checked against the raw pages. Es and it names are machine drafts (abrótano hembra is the starter-list name; cipresillo and cipressina are names I know people use, not sourced)."
      },
